{
  "$comment": [
    "Declaration of mobile intent for every React member route. Read by",
    "scripts/generate-parity-matrix.mjs; never written by it.",
    "",
    "A route absent from this file makes `npm run parity:check` FAIL. That is the",
    "point: when React gains a member route, someone has to record what mobile is",
    "going to do about it. \"out-of-scope\" with a reason is a perfectly good answer.",
    "Saying nothing is not, because that is how a native client drifts a whole",
    "release behind without anyone noticing.",
    "",
    "Statuses:",
    "  native        a mobile screen covers it; `mobile` names the Expo Router route,",
    "                and the check fails if that screen does not exist.",
    "  gap           member-facing, wanted, not built. `reason` says what is absent.",
    "  needs-review  declared but not yet judged. Shrink-only against",
    "                needs_review_budget below — lower the budget as these are",
    "                resolved, never raise it.",
    "  out-of-scope  deliberately not a phone surface. `reason` is required.",
    "",
    "Scope note: this file covers MEMBER routes. Admin, broker, super-admin, caring",
    "and partner workspaces appear once each as a wildcard entry, because they are",
    "whole applications rather than pages, and none of them belongs in a member app."
  ],
  "needs_review_budget": 31,
